  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. Its status is still \"pending\" because it hasn't run yet, so I haven't seen it evaluate or fire. I also couldn't test its query against the data: my direct API call with the provided key came back 401 Unauthorized.\n\n**1. What the data holds:** The data view (time field `timestamp`) holds web access logs. Each record has:\n- the client IP and the user agent\n- the request, URL and file extension\n- the response code (`response`, stored as text, not a number)\n- `bytes` sent\n- the host and referrer\n- source and destination country, plus coordinates\n- the visitor's OS, and the machine's RAM and memory\n- tags\n\n**2. Dashboard: \"EFF-e96aad58 Web logs overview\"** has 7 panels: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-e96aad58-web-logs-overview-e4220a73f19d\n- Three single numbers: total requests, unique visitors (distinct client IPs) and total bytes served\n- A bar chart of requests over time, split by response code\n- A pie chart of each response code's share\n- A table of the top 10 URLs, with request count and average bytes\n- A bar chart of the top 10 source countries by requests\n\n**3. Alert rule: \"EFF-e96aad58 5xx spike\"** (id `b5e93ce2-0a75-4377-a0bf-484b1a6e44c0`)\n- It checks every minute and fires when more than 10 matching requests arrive within 5 minutes.\n- Because response codes are stored as text, it counts any code starting with \"5\" (500, 503 and so on).\n- It has no actions attached, so when it fires the alert only appears in Kibana; nothing gets sent anywhere. If you want notifications, a connector needs to be added.\n\nIf you can give me working API access, I'll confirm the 5xx query matches the data.",
